{
  "id": "forget-cue",
  "term": "forget cue",
  "definition": "A forget cue is an instruction given after learning an initial list in the list-method directed forgetting paradigm that tells participants to forget that earlier material. Compared with a remember cue, it is typically linked to poorer recall of the first list and better recall of the second list.",
